		<traitlist>
			<id-00001>
				<name type="string">Ability Score Increase</name>
				<text type="formattedtext">
					<p>Your Wisdom score increases by 2, and your Intelligence score increases by 1.</p>
				</text>
			</id-00001>
			<id-00002>
				<name type="string">Size</name>
				<text type="formattedtext">
					<p>Hierarch octons of Mechanus are Large, but Mandurdron is a field-deployed unit compacted to Medium size.</p>
				</text>
			</id-00002>
			<id-00003>
				<name type="string">Speed</name>
				<text type="formattedtext">
					<p>Your base walking speed is 30 feet, and you have a swimming speed of 30 feet.</p>
				</text>
			</id-00003>
			<id-00004>
				<name type="string">Living Construct</name>
				<text type="formattedtext">
					<p>You don't need to eat, drink, or breathe, and you are immune to disease. You have advantage on saving throws against poison and resistance to poison damage. You don't sleep; you finish a long rest by spending 6 hours in an inactive, motionless state, during which you remain aware of your surroundings.</p>
				</text>
			</id-00004>
			<id-00005>
				<name type="string">All-Around Vision</name>
				<text type="formattedtext">
					<p>A ring of eyes circles your hull. You have darkvision out to 60 feet and proficiency in the Perception skill, and you can't be surprised while you are conscious and not blinded.</p>
				</text>
			</id-00005>
			<id-00006>
				<name type="string">Axiomatic Mind</name>
				<text type="formattedtext">
					<p>You have advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can't compel you to act against your alignment or your standing orders.</p>
				</text>
			</id-00006>
			<id-00007>
				<name type="string">Hierarchy Link</name>
				<text type="formattedtext">
					<p>You can speak telepathically to any creature you can see within 60 feet of you that understands at least one language. The creature can answer you through the link.</p>
				</text>
			</id-00007>
			<id-00008>
				<name type="string">Clockwork Cadence</name>
				<text type="formattedtext">
					<p>Modrons act on a fixed schedule. When you roll initiative, you can choose to use 10 + your Dexterity modifier as your result instead of rolling.</p>
				</text>
			</id-00008>
			<id-00009>
				<name type="string">Tentacle Ring</name>
				<text type="formattedtext">
					<p>Your eight tentacles are natural weapons with a reach of 10 feet, which you can use to make unarmed strikes. On a hit, a tentacle deals bludgeoning damage equal to 1d6 + your Strength modifier. You can use your tentacles to manipulate objects, but you can wield no more than one weapon or shield in them at a time.</p>
				</text>
			</id-00009>
			<id-00010>
				<name type="string">Octon Innate Magic</name>
				<text type="formattedtext">
					<p>You can cast water walk on yourself at will, without expending a spell slot. You can also cast detect evil and good once, and you regain the ability to do so when you finish a long rest. Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for these spells.</p>
				</text>
			</id-00010>
			<id-00011>
				<name type="string">Hover Field</name>
				<text type="formattedtext">
					<p>As a bonus action, you can gain a flying speed of 30 feet for 1 minute, and you can hover. Once you use this trait, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest.</p>
				</text>
			</id-00011>
			<id-00012>
				<name type="string">Disintegration</name>
				<text type="formattedtext">
					<p>If you die, your body disintegrates into dust, leaving behind your gear. Spells that restore life can still return you if cast on your dust.</p>
				</text>
			</id-00012>
			<id-00013>
				<name type="string">Languages</name>
				<text type="formattedtext">
					<p>You can speak, read, and write Common and Modron.</p>
				</text>
			</id-00013>
		</traitlist>
		<featurelist>
			<id-00001>
				<name type="string">Spellcasting</name>
				<text type="formattedtext">
					<p>You prepare cleric spells using Wisdom (spell save DC 17, spell attack +9). You can prepare 16 cleric spells per long rest, plus your domain spells, which are always prepared.</p>
				</text>
			</id-00001>
			<id-00002>
				<name type="string">Channel Divinity (2/rest)</name>
				<text type="formattedtext">
					<p>You can channel divine energy twice between rests, choosing Turn Undead or Sector Command each time. You regain expended uses when you finish a short or long rest.</p>
				</text>
			</id-00002>
			<id-00003>
				<name type="string">Channel Divinity: Turn Undead</name>
				<text type="formattedtext">
					<p>As an action, each undead within 30 feet that can see or hear you must make a Wisdom save or be turned for 1 minute or until it takes damage.</p>
				</text>
			</id-00003>
			<id-00004>
				<name type="string">Destroy Undead (CR 2)</name>
				<text type="formattedtext">
					<p>When an undead of CR 2 or lower fails its save against your Turn Undead, it is destroyed instead.</p>
				</text>
			</id-00004>
			<id-00005>
				<name type="string">Divine Intervention</name>
				<text type="formattedtext">
					<p>As an action, call on Primus for aid. Roll percentile dice; if you roll 11 or lower, the intervention occurs. Once it succeeds, you can't use this feature for 7 days; otherwise, you can try again after a long rest.</p>
				</text>
			</id-00005>
			<id-00006>
				<name type="string">Ability Score Improvements</name>
				<text type="formattedtext">
					<p>Level 4: Wisdom +2. Level 8: Wisdom +1, Constitution +1.</p>
				</text>
			</id-00006>
			<id-00007>
				<name type="string">Hierarch Domain</name>
				<text type="formattedtext">
					<p>Your god is the Great Wheel's engine of law, embodied in Primus. You are an octon: a governor of one sector of Mechanus, directing the units beneath you.</p>
				</text>
			</id-00007>
			<id-00008>
				<name type="string">Hierarch Domain Spells</name>
				<text type="formattedtext">
					<p>Always prepared: 1st command, shield of faith; 3rd hold person, zone of truth; 5th clairvoyance, haste; 7th compulsion, dimension door; 9th telekinesis, wall of force.</p>
				</text>
			</id-00008>
			<id-00009>
				<name type="string">Bonus Proficiencies</name>
				<text type="formattedtext">
					<p>At 1st level, you gain proficiency with heavy armor and the History skill.</p>
				</text>
			</id-00009>
			<id-00010>
				<name type="string">Chain of Command</name>
				<text type="formattedtext">
					<p>At 1st level, as a bonus action, you issue a directive to one ally within 60 feet who can hear you or is linked to you telepathically. That ally can immediately use its reaction to make one weapon attack or move up to half its speed without provoking opportunity attacks. You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (5), and regain all uses when you finish a long rest.</p>
				</text>
			</id-00010>
			<id-00011>
				<name type="string">Channel Divinity: Sector Command</name>
				<text type="formattedtext">
					<p>At 2nd level, as an action, you speak a single directive to any number of creatures of your choice within 30 feet. Each must make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failure, it follows the directive on its next turn, as the command spell. Creatures immune to being charmed are unaffected.</p>
				</text>
			</id-00011>
			<id-00012>
				<name type="string">Lawful Ward</name>
				<text type="formattedtext">
					<p>At 6th level, you have resistance to psychic damage. When a creature you can see within 30 feet must make a saving throw against being charmed or frightened, you can use your reaction to give it advantage on the save.</p>
				</text>
			</id-00012>
			<id-00013>
				<name type="string">Octon's Lash</name>
				<text type="formattedtext">
					<p>At 8th level, once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with a weapon attack or tentacle, you can deal an extra 1d8 force damage to it. The extra damage increases to 2d8 at 14th level.</p>
				</text>
			</id-00013>
		</featurelist>
